#=======================================================================
# 8. REFINEMENT DATA
_refine_special_details
; Carbon and Nitrogen atoms were refined isotropically due to the 
  heavily disordered nature of the cations. The IM cations were refined as
  6-atom hexagonal molecules akin to sym-triazine, with the C-C and the C-N
  bond distances restrained to 1.38(1) Angstrom. Although crude, this method
  is suitable for fitting a pentagonal molecule through a 3-fold rotation 
  axis. The method was adopted from Zhang, W.; Cai, Y.; Xiong, R.-G.;
  Yoshikawa, H.; Awaga, K., Angew. Chem.,Int. Ed. 2010, 49, 6608-6610.
  The occupancy of the C and N atoms was set to 2/3 and 1/3, respectively
  to reflect the correct stoichiometry. The thermal parameters of the IM 
  molecules were restrained so that each cation has the same Uiso.
;
